    <string name="tutorial_done">Done</string>
    <string name="tutorial_neck_title">Neck</string>
    <string name="tutorial_neck_text">Measure just below the Adam\'s apple. Let the tape slope slightly down towards the front.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_waist_men_title">Waist (men)</string>
    <string name="tutorial_waist_men_text">Measure around the belly at the belly button, after breathing out normally. Don\'t pull in your belly.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_waist_women_title">Waist (women)</string>
    <string name="tutorial_waist_women_text">Measure the waist at its narrowest point, usually a little above the belly button, after breathing out normally.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_hips_title">Hips (women)</string>
    <string name="tutorial_hips_text">Measure around the hips at the widest point of the buttocks, with your feet together.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_tips_title">Tips</string>
    <string name="tutorial_tips_text">• Measure in the morning, before eating.
• Stand relaxed and don\'t pull in your belly.
• Keep the tape flat and level, snug but not pressing into the skin.
• Measure each place 3 times and use the average.

This is an estimate. It can be off by a few percent, but it is good for following the trend.</string>
